      "title": "Thick smoke seen near Riyadh airport after air-raid alerts in Saudi capital",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/19/saudi-arabia-riyadh-airport",
      "description": "<p>Authorities also issued warnings for Jeddah and Yanbu, a major industrial port and home to vital oil facilities</p><p>Flames and a large plume of black smoke were seen rising above Riyadh airport in Saudi Arabia on Saturday after the government sent air-raid alerts to citizens by phone overnight warning of aerial attacks.</p><p>Explosions were heard in the capital and firefighters battled to extinguish the flames of a burning fuel tank emblazoned with the logo of the Saudi oil company Aramco near the city’s King Khalid international airport.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/19/saudi-arabia-riyadh-airport\">Continue reading...</a>",
